Subject: Retain A Shape's Predecessor So Transitions Survive

What this does
  `JSShape` gains `parent`, a strong reference to the shape it was cloned from,
  set by `add_property`'s clone arm and released with the shape. A construction
  path that was walked once can then be resolved from the transition table
  instead of being cloned again.

Why we need it
  A construction path arrives at a new shape by cloning the shape it extends,
  and records that transition under the successor. The predecessor was reachable
  only from the same table, which holds no reference, so it died with its last
  object and every later object on the same path paid the clone again.

What it adds
  One pointer per shape, marked and released with the shape. The parent graph is
  acyclic by construction -- a parent always existed before its child -- so the
  release recurses along a bounded chain. MEASURED on-device, shape clones per
  Octane run: typescript 7,017,436 -> 29,514 (238x), while the other seven rows
  are unchanged (splay 65, pdfjs 7,586, deltablue 149, richards 103, crypto 161,
  gbemu 621, navierstokes 61). Score, same-binary over six runs: typescript
  +4.55% (7,971 -> 8,334, the two arms not overlapping); 8-row geomean +0.40%.

  COST, stated because it is the opposite of the source patch's claim that peak
  heap goes down: retaining predecessors keeps them allocated, so on typescript
  the live shapes go 1,252 -> 3,283 and shape bytes 295,024 -> 2,005,472
  (+1.7 MB, +580%), making total malloc 4.93 MB -> 6.66 MB (+35%) on that row. A
  workload that creates and drops shapes measures +0.2%, and the other seven
  rows clone nothing extra, so the cost is confined to the clone-heavy workloads
  that also gain.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 72fcc50..df69918 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -1337,6 +1337,7 @@ struct JSShape {
     int prop_count; /* include deleted properties */
     int deleted_prop_count;
     JSShape *shape_hash_next; /* in JSRuntime.shape_hash[h] list */
+    JSShape *parent; /* strong reference to the shape this one was derived from */
     JSObject *proto;
     uint32_t hash_table[]; /* prop_hash_mask + 1 elements, then prop[prop_size] */
 };
@@ -6438,6 +6439,7 @@ static inline JSShape *js_new_shape_nohash(JSContext *ctx, JSObject *proto,
     sh->prop_count = 0;
     sh->deleted_prop_count = 0;
     sh->is_hashed = false;
+    sh->parent = NULL;
     return sh;
 }
 
@@ -6525,6 +6527,7 @@ static JSShape *js_clone_shape(JSContext *ctx, JSShape *sh1)
     JS_REF_COUNT(sh) = 1;
     add_gc_object(ctx->rt, &sh->header, JS_GC_OBJ_TYPE_SHAPE);
     sh->is_hashed = false;
+    sh->parent = NULL;
     if (sh->proto) {
         js_dup(JS_MKPTR(JS_TAG_OBJECT, sh->proto));
     }
@@ -6558,6 +6561,13 @@ static void js_free_shape0(JSRuntime *rt, JSShape *sh)
         pr++;
     }
     remove_gc_object(&sh->header);
+    {
+        JSShape *parent = sh->parent;
+
+        sh->parent = NULL;
+        if (parent)
+            js_free_shape(rt, parent);
+    }
     js_free_rt(rt, get_alloc_from_shape(sh));
 }
 
@@ -8567,6 +8577,9 @@ static void mark_children(JSRuntime *rt, JSGCObjectHeader *gp,
             if (sh->proto != NULL) {
                 mark_func(rt, &sh->proto->header);
             }
+            if (sh->parent != NULL) {
+                mark_func(rt, &sh->parent->header);
+            }
         }
         break;
     case JS_GC_OBJ_TYPE_JS_CONTEXT:
@@ -11509,6 +11522,7 @@ static JSProperty *add_property(JSContext *ctx,
             new_sh = js_clone_shape(ctx, sh);
             if (!new_sh)
                 return NULL;
+            new_sh->parent = js_dup_shape(sh);
             /* hash the cloned shape */
             new_sh->is_hashed = true;
             js_shape_hash_link(ctx->rt, new_sh);
